 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:black;margin-bottom:6.0pt;line-height:11.55pt;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3'><span style='font-family:"Tamil Sangam MN"'>PLDA:
     Parallel Latent Dirichlet Allocation for Large-scale Applications, Y.
     Wang, Hongjie, Bai, M. Stanton, Wen-Yen Chen, Edward Y. Chang,
     International Conference on Algorithmic Applications in Management, June
     2009.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:black;margin-bottom:6.0pt;line-height:11.55pt;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3'><span style='font-family:"Tamil Sangam MN"'>PLDA+:
     Parallel Latent Dirichlet Allocation with Data Placement and Pipeline
     Processing, Z. Liu, Y. Zhang, EY Chang, and M. Sun, ACM Transactions on
     Intelligent Systems and Technology 2(3), 2011.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:black;margin-bottom:6.0pt;line-height:11.55pt;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3'><span style='font-family:"Tamil Sangam MN"'>Parallel
     Spectral Clustering in Distributed Systems, WY Chen, Y. Song, H. Bai, CJ
     Lin, and EY Chang, IEEE PAMI, 2011.<o:p></o:p></span></li>
 <li class=MsoNormal style='color:black;margin-bottom:6.0pt;line-height:11.55pt;
     mso-list:l0 level1 lfo3;background:white'><span style='font-family:"Tamil Sangam MN"'>Scalable
     ML open source, patents, and Google QA product are listed below:<o:p></o:p></span></li>
</ol>

<p class=MsoNormal style='margin-top:0in;margin-right:0in;margin-bottom:6.0pt;
margin-left:.75in;text-indent:-.25in;line-height:11.55pt;mso-list:l0 level2 lfo3;
